    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\dfrac{\\sqrt{15}-\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}+1}{8}$\n\nFactorise the denominator as $(1+\\sqrt{3})(1+\\sqrt{5})$, then use both conjugates.",
      "worked": "Factorise by grouping:\n$$\\begin{align*}1+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}&=(1+\\sqrt{3})+\\sqrt{5}(1+\\sqrt{3})\\\\1+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}&=(1+\\sqrt{3})(1+\\sqrt{5}).\\end{align*}$$\nMultiply by the conjugate of each factor:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{1+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}}&=\\frac{1}{(1+\\sqrt{3})(1+\\sqrt{5})}\\times\\frac{(1-\\sqrt{3})(1-\\sqrt{5})}{(1-\\sqrt{3})(1-\\sqrt{5})}\\\\\\frac{1}{1+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}}&=\\frac{(1-\\sqrt{3})(1-\\sqrt{5})}{(1-3)(1-5)}\\\\\\frac{1}{1+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}}&=\\frac{1-\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{15}}{8}\\\\\\frac{1}{1+\\sqrt{3}+\\sqrt{5}+\\sqrt{15}}&=\\frac{\\sqrt{15}-\\sqrt{5}-\\sqrt{3}+1}{8}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
